An archetype, not a replica
---------------------------

This cartridge models a FAMILY — two rigid half-frames on a fold axis along the
long edge, one continuous display folded inward across both of them, a second
display on the outside of one half — which is ours to license. It does not model
any manufacturer's product.

Named devices appear only as PRESETS. A preset is a set of numbers, and every
number in it is either:

  * a DIMENSION THE MANUFACTURER PUBLISHED, carried from Telesia's device
    geometry registry (`data/registry/device-geometry.json`), where each value
    records its source tier, URL, retrieval date and the line it was quoted
    from; or

  * a value DERIVED from such a dimension by an archetype rule that is OURS and
    is written down (docs/README.md, "Archetype derivation rules"); or

  * an ARCHETYPE DEFAULT that is ours outright.

Nothing else. In particular this cartridge reproduces no logo, no wordmark, no
badge, no colourway, no textures, no vents, no parting lines, no button glyphs,
and no surface detail of any kind beyond what a published outline, a published
display active area and a published port list imply. It is deliberately a pair
of plain slabs: the shape you get is the archetype's, not the product's.

**A preset is a fit envelope, not a likeness.** It is there so a cradle, a dock,
a travel shell or a repair fixture can be built to the right size.


What is SOURCED here that the clamshell cartridge had to guess
--------------------------------------------------------------

Worth stating plainly, because it is what makes this family's presets stronger
than the clamshell's: manufacturers in this family publish BOTH a closed and an
open envelope, and three of this model's load-bearing numbers fall straight out
of that pair rather than out of a rule of ours.

  * `half_thickness` is the published OPEN depth. The open body is one half.
  * The hinge gap is the published closed depth LESS TWICE the published open
    depth. It is recorded per preset under `registry.hinge_gap_mm`.
  * `camera_half_width` is the published open width LESS the published closed
    width. A book fold closes because one half is narrower than the other, and
    that difference is the manufacturer's own arithmetic.

On 26 of the 27 presets the model's closed AND open bounding boxes reproduce
the published figures to 0.000 mm on every axis. The exception is noted below.


What is ours, specifically
--------------------------

These are the archetype's own decisions. They are not, and must not be read as,
statements about any device:

  * Corner radius. No manufacturer in this family publishes one — 0 of the
    registry's 84 devices — so every corner radius here is ours. So is the
    decision to round only the OPENING edge and leave the spine square in plan.
  * The crease relief: its radius, its running clearance and how far it runs.
    The hinge leaf in its entirety. A real free-stop teardrop hinge is a
    multi-link mechanism no published source describes for any device in this
    family.
  * Display recess depth, and where each display sits within its frame (the
    presets centre it; no manufacturer publishes a bezel split). Where a display
    active area is unresolved in the registry, the WINDOW is the published
    envelope inset by an archetype bezel — the envelope is the manufacturer's,
    the inset is ours, and the preset names it as a fallback.
  * The camera island in its entirety: its size, its position, the number of
    apertures and their size. The registry records no camera geometry for any
    device in this family. It is also modelled as a RECESS rather than a raised
    bump, because every depth published in this family excludes the camera bump
    and none publishes its height — raising one would invent a dimension.
  * Every button's size, position and count. The registry's only control kind in
    this family is `fingerprint`, on 4 of 28 devices, and it records no button
    geometry.
  * The port opening sizes and where along a face they sit. Only the PRESENCE of
    a port is sourced.
  * The card tray in its entirety apart from its presence.
  * The speaker grille in its entirety.


Where the published numbers disagree with each other
-----------------------------------------------------

One device's two published figures cannot both hold for a body of two equal
halves, and this cartridge says so rather than quietly splitting the difference:

  * OPPO Find N3 (`oppo-find-n3`) — OPPO publishes a closed depth of 11.7 mm and
    an open depth of 5.9 mm; twice 5.9 is 11.8. The CLOSED envelope is the one
    this cartridge asserts against, so the half thickness is derived from it
    (5.825 mm) and the preset names that as a fallback. The model's open depth is
    therefore 0.075 mm from OPPO's published figure, which is reported in the
    verification table rather than hidden. OPPO also publishes no open width or
    open height for this model, so its camera half falls back to the cover half's
    width and its open envelope is a model output, not a device claim.


Devices with no preset
----------------------

One device the registry files in this family has no preset, because its closed
envelope is unresolved and this cartridge will not invent one:

  * Samsung Galaxy Z Fold Special Edition (`samsung-galaxy-z-fold-special-edition`)
    — Samsung's Korean launch release gives a closed thickness (10.6 mm) and a
    mass, but no closed height or width and no open envelope at all.

`null = unresolved, never guessed`.


